    "## 3. PBSMT Project Setup (Moses EMS)\n",
    "\n",
    "We use Moses' **Experiment Management System (EMS)** — a single `config.baseline` file plus `experiment.perl` drives corpus prep, GIZA/MGIZA alignment, language-model training, phrase/reordering table building, MERT tuning, decoding, and BLEU scoring. Reference scripts (`config.baseline`, `generate_configs.pl`, `run-baseline.pl`, the SGM-conversion scripts) came from the instructor's MTRSS repository and were adapted with our own machine paths and language pair (`my`/`ph` instead of `my`/`rk`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "42daccc6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%bash\n",
    "cd ~/Documents/Assignment6/g2p-smt\n",
    "cp -r MTRSS/pbsmt/config.baseline MTRSS/pbsmt/generate_configs.pl MTRSS/pbsmt/run-baseline.pl pbsmt/\n",
    "ls pbsmt\n"
   ]
  },
  {
