   "source": [
    "### 5.1 Errors encountered and fixes\n",
    "\n",
    "Running this pipeline from scratch surfaced three errors, consistent with the kind of path/dependency issues flagged in the instructor's own tutorial notebook:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Error 1 — `Can't exec \"convert\"`**\n",
    "ImageMagick's `convert` is used only for the optional `-no-graph` visualization step. Harmless; safely ignored since `-no-graph` was already passed to `experiment.perl`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Error 2 — MGIZA alignment-merge crash**\n",
    "```\n",
    "Executing: .../merge_alignment.py ...\n",
    "/usr/bin/env: 'python': No such file or directory\n",
    "Exit code: 127\n",
    "```\n",
    "`merge_alignment.py` shells out to `python`, but only `python3` exists on Ubuntu 24.04+. Fixed by installing a `python -> python3` shim:\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "sudo apt install python-is-python3\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Error 3 — NIST BLEU scorer Unicode regex failure**\n",
    "```\n",
    "Can't find Unicode property definition \\\"Line_Break\\\" in regex; ... \\p{Line_Break}\\p{Zl}\n",
    "  at .../scripts/generic/mteval-v13a.pl line 950.\n",
    "```\n",
    "The bundled `mteval-v13a.pl` (NIST/IBM-style BLEU) is incompatible with the modern Perl Unicode tables on this machine. Fixed, as anticipated in the tutorial's own notes, by switching scoring to **`multi-bleu.perl`** — uncommenting the `multi-bleu = ...` line in `config.baseline` and re-running."
   ]
  },
